SeSAMe preprocessing and bundled array references
------------------------------------------------
- SeSAMe: Wanding Zhou and contributors; https://github.com/zwdzwd/sesame
  Package license: MIT (2024, Wanding Zhou). The IDAT workflow calls the installed
  SeSAMe package; it does not vendor its implementation.
- sesameData 1.24.0: Wanding Zhou and contributors;
  https://bioconductor.org/packages/sesameData/ ; package license: Artistic-2.0.
  A copy is included at epigenetic-clocks/data/SESAME_DATA_LICENSE.txt.
- epigenetic-clocks/data/sesame-reference-cache.tar.gz contains a selected,
  unmodified set of public sesameData/ExperimentHub annotation objects and the
  public Hub metadata needed for offline lookup. Only the cache registry is
  trimmed and its file paths made relative for relocation. It is a subset of
  sesameData resources, not a distribution of the full sesameData package.
- Resource titles, ExperimentHub accessions, sizes, package versions and SHA-256
  hashes are recorded in epigenetic-clocks/data/sesame-resources.json. Original
  resource files remain byte-for-byte as cached from ExperimentHub.
- SeSAMe paper: Zhou W, Triche TJ Jr, Laird PW, Shen H. "SeSAMe: reducing
  artifactual detection of DNA methylation by Infinium BeadChips in genomic
  deletions." Nucleic Acids Research, 2018. DOI: 10.1093/nar/gky691.

